ind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-55066940-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>55066940</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1043372A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>CLARIANT INT LTD</name><address><country>CH</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURASE NAOKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CLARIANT INTERNATIONAL LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURASE, NAOKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURASE NAOKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURASE, NAOKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A coating composition which, when applied to a paper surface, gives a coated paper excellent in various properties including gloss, water resistance, solvent resistance, heat resistance, thermal blocking resistance, and ink receptivity and also in suitability for recycling. The coating composition comprises: a hydrosol obtained by dispersing particles of a synthetic resin having carboxyl and alkoxysilyl groups into water and neutralizing the emulsion with an alkali; and a colloidal silica.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Composition de couchage qui, appliquée à la surface d'un papier, donne un papier couché possédant d'excellentes propriétés telles que brillant, résistance à l'eau, résistance aux solvants, résistance à la chaleur, résistance au blocage thermique, réceptivité à l'encre et aptitude au recyclage. La composition comprend un hydrosol, que l'on obtient en dispersant dans l'eau des particules de résine synthétique contenant des groupes carboxyle et alcoxysilyle, puis en neutralisant l'émulsion avec un alcali; et une silice colloïdale.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>